1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,623
Late May, 1951. Hwachon, Gangwon Province.

2
00:00:05,729 --> 00:00:07,599
On a vast reservoir buried in

3
00:00:07,619 --> 00:00:09,636
thick fog, something began to

4
00:00:09,656 --> 00:00:12,413
rise to the surface, one by one.

5
00:00:12,756 --> 00:00:14,539
The blue lake had turned red,

6
00:00:14,559 --> 00:00:16,985
and bodies were drifting on the water.

7
00:00:17,052 --> 00:00:19,126
That is how one South Korean company

8
00:00:19,146 --> 00:00:20,845
commander, advancing toward this

9
00:00:20,865 --> 00:00:23,142
place, later remembered the lake.

10
00:00:23,344 --> 00:00:25,202
Korean official histories record

11
00:00:25,222 --> 00:00:27,410
more than thirty thousand Chinese

12
00:00:27,430 --> 00:00:29,959
killed or captured in this area.

13
00:00:29,991 --> 00:00:32,065
They had an escape route to the north.

14
00:00:32,085 --> 00:00:33,676
So why did they end up

15
00:00:33,696 --> 00:00:35,587
trapped at the edge of this lake?

16
00:00:35,771 --> 00:00:37,654
The Battle of Paro Lake.

17
00:00:37,693 --> 00:00:39,641
This is the story of the ROK 6th

18
00:00:39,661 --> 00:00:42,043
Division's sixty-kilometer pursuit,

19
00:00:42,063 --> 00:00:44,149
rising from the depths of defeat,

20
00:00:44,169 --> 00:00:46,437
and of how a reservoir came to be called

21
00:00:46,457 --> 00:00:48,962
the Lake of the Defeated Barbarians.

22
00:00:49,309 --> 00:00:51,027
The 6th Division had always been

23
00:00:51,047 --> 00:00:53,052
a unit with a special pride.

24
00:00:53,191 --> 00:00:56,598
On October 26th, 1950, the first unit

25
00:00:56,618 --> 00:00:59,124
among all South Korean and UN forces to

26
00:00:59,144 --> 00:01:01,720
reach the Yalu River and scoop up its water

27
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:04,807
was the 6th Division's 7th Regiment.

28
00:01:05,002 --> 00:01:06,216
But half a year later,

29
00:01:06,236 --> 00:01:09,311
that division met a humiliating defeat.

30
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:12,376
On the night of April 22nd, 1951,

31
00:01:12,396 --> 00:01:15,596
the Chinese launched their April Offensive.

32
00:01:15,795 --> 00:01:18,170
Holding Sachang-ni, west of Hwachon,

33
00:01:18,190 --> 00:01:21,039
the ROK 6th Division collapsed

34
00:01:21,059 --> 00:01:23,019
under the very first blow.

35
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:25,035
Its men scattered over the mountains,

36
00:01:25,055 --> 00:01:27,402
abandoning their equipment and guns,

37
00:01:27,422 --> 00:01:29,452
and for a time the division all but

38
00:01:29,472 --> 00:01:31,862
ceased to exist as a fighting force.

39
00:01:32,065 --> 00:01:33,682
The flanks of the U.S. Marines

40
00:01:33,702 --> 00:01:35,162
and Commonwealth troops fighting

41
00:01:35,182 --> 00:01:37,870
alongside were laid wide open.

42
00:01:37,997 --> 00:01:40,095
American commanders reportedly went so

43
00:01:40,115 --> 00:01:42,132
far as to say the division had,

44
00:01:42,152 --> 00:01:45,522
for all practical purposes, ceased to exist.

45
00:01:45,718 --> 00:01:48,126
Eighth Army commander Van Fleet and UN

46
00:01:48,146 --> 00:01:50,823
commander Ridgway are said to have confronted

47
00:01:50,843 --> 00:01:53,168
President Syngman Rhee hard over

48
00:01:53,188 --> 00:01:55,614
the leadership of the South Korean army.

49
00:01:55,652 --> 00:01:57,055
The 6th Division's name

50
00:01:57,075 --> 00:01:58,889
had sunk to rock bottom.

51
00:01:59,079 --> 00:02:00,015
Division commander,

52
00:02:00,035 --> 00:02:02,507
Brigadier General Chang Do-yong.

53
00:02:02,643 --> 00:02:04,581
He gathered his scattered men and

54
00:02:04,601 --> 00:02:07,125
demanded of his officers a vow: in the

55
00:02:07,145 --> 00:02:09,491
next fight, they would not fall back.

56
00:02:09,671 --> 00:02:11,427
One month later, the chance

57
00:02:11,447 --> 00:02:13,497
for redemption arrived.

58
00:02:13,615 --> 00:02:16,088
On May 16th, the Chinese launched

59
00:02:16,108 --> 00:02:17,948
another massive offensive.

60
00:02:18,148 --> 00:02:20,279
Toward the 6th Division, holding the

61
00:02:20,299 --> 00:02:22,829
Yongmun Mountain area in Yangpyong,

62
00:02:22,849 --> 00:02:26,436
came three divisions of the Chinese 63rd Army.

63
00:02:26,491 --> 00:02:31,069
The 187th, 188th and 189th.

64
00:02:31,089 --> 00:02:33,057
Three divisions against one.

65
00:02:33,261 --> 00:02:35,569
The Chinese command was confident.

66
00:02:35,649 --> 00:02:37,655
The enemy in front of them was the very

67
00:02:37,675 --> 00:02:40,739
division they had smashed just a month before.

68
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:42,419
By their reckoning, it would

69
00:02:42,439 --> 00:02:44,349
be over in a single night.

70
00:02:44,515 --> 00:02:46,209
On the night of May 18th,

71
00:02:46,229 --> 00:02:49,088
red flares rose one after another above

72
00:02:49,108 --> 00:02:51,410
the ridges in front of Yongmunsan.

73
00:02:51,554 --> 00:02:54,368
Moments later, the shouts of thousands echoed

74
00:02:54,388 --> 00:02:56,626
down the mountains out of the darkness.

75
00:02:56,822 --> 00:02:58,849
The division had pushed only its 2nd

76
00:02:58,869 --> 00:03:01,308
Regiment forward to an outpost line,

77
00:03:01,328 --> 00:03:03,459
keeping the 7th and 19th on

78
00:03:03,479 --> 00:03:06,088
the main line of resistance behind.

79
00:03:06,205 --> 00:03:09,420
On May 18th, Chinese company-sized forces

80
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,323
tried several times to cross the river by day,

81
00:03:12,343 --> 00:03:14,597
and every attempt was beaten back.

82
00:03:14,685 --> 00:03:17,214
Then before dawn on the 19th, mistaking

83
00:03:17,234 --> 00:03:19,240
the outpost for the main line,

84
00:03:19,260 --> 00:03:21,847
the Chinese began throwing in the main bodies of

85
00:03:21,867 --> 00:03:26,435
the 187th and 188th Divisions at once.

86
00:03:26,603 --> 00:03:28,894
Night after night came wave attacks,

87
00:03:28,914 --> 00:03:31,192
led by bugles and gongs.

88
00:03:31,316 --> 00:03:33,219
Even surrounded, the 2nd Regiment

89
00:03:33,239 --> 00:03:35,029
would not give up its positions,

90
00:03:35,049 --> 00:03:38,045
while artillery rained down without pause

91
00:03:38,065 --> 00:03:40,313
on the Chinese climbing the slopes.

92
00:03:40,506 --> 00:03:43,202
As the line held, the enemy wore down,

93
00:03:43,222 --> 00:03:46,797
and their ammunition and food began to run out.

94
00:03:46,895 --> 00:03:49,232
Then on May 20th, the 6th Division

95
00:03:49,252 --> 00:03:51,444
finally turned to the counterattack.

96
00:03:51,629 --> 00:03:53,434
The very division that had collapsed

97
00:03:53,454 --> 00:03:55,654
at Sachang-ni a month earlier was

98
00:03:55,674 --> 00:03:58,192
now driving back three divisions.

99
00:03:58,282 --> 00:03:59,856
This fight would come to be called

100
00:03:59,876 --> 00:04:02,378
the Great Victory of Yongmunsan.

101
00:04:02,583 --> 00:04:04,805
But the real story begins here.

102
00:04:04,930 --> 00:04:06,789
Because against a crumbling enemy,

103
00:04:06,809 --> 00:04:10,066
the 6th Division's pursuit was about to begin.

104
00:04:10,391 --> 00:04:11,774
The nameless records left

105
00:04:11,794 --> 00:04:13,276
on these battlefields.

106
00:04:13,331 --> 00:04:14,654
So that we can keep telling this

107
00:04:14,674 --> 00:04:16,919
desperate history to the end, please

108
00:04:16,939 --> 00:04:19,411
join us with a subscribe and a like.

109
00:04:19,751 --> 00:04:22,772
And on May 20th, the bloody pursuit began.

110
00:04:22,965 --> 00:04:26,083
In late May, UN forces counterattacked

111
00:04:26,103 --> 00:04:28,245
all along the central front.

112
00:04:28,402 --> 00:04:30,988
U.S. IX Corps, to which the 6th Division

113
00:04:31,008 --> 00:04:33,299
belonged, pushed north together

114
00:04:33,319 --> 00:04:36,623
with the U.S. 24th Division, the ROK 2nd

115
00:04:36,643 --> 00:04:39,197
Division and the U.S. 7th Division.

116
00:04:39,398 --> 00:04:41,251
In truth, the Chinese had put

117
00:04:41,271 --> 00:04:43,186
their main weight in the May Offensive

118
00:04:43,206 --> 00:04:44,973
into the eastern mountains.

119
00:04:45,063 --> 00:04:46,773
The 63rd Army that hit the 6th

120
00:04:46,793 --> 00:04:48,741
Division was a supporting attack.

121
00:04:48,796 --> 00:04:51,200
But when that supporting attack collapsed first,

122
00:04:51,220 --> 00:04:54,088
a huge gap opened in the central front.

123
00:04:54,270 --> 00:04:57,263
The 6th Division's road ran from Yangpyong

124
00:04:57,283 --> 00:04:59,778
through Kapyong and Chunchon,

125
00:04:59,798 --> 00:05:02,441
all the way to the Hwachon power plant.

126
00:05:02,610 --> 00:05:04,468
Mountain country stretching some sixty

127
00:05:04,488 --> 00:05:07,020
kilometers, even as the crow flies.

128
00:05:07,209 --> 00:05:08,221
The soldiers fought by

129
00:05:08,241 --> 00:05:09,962
day and marched by night.

130
00:05:10,131 --> 00:05:12,945
With ammunition and rice balls on their backs,

131
00:05:12,965 --> 00:05:15,335
they chased the enemy's tail along mountain

132
00:05:15,355 --> 00:05:18,490
trails that barely appeared on any map.

133
00:05:18,687 --> 00:05:21,650
Abandoned carts, rifles, and burned bundles

134
00:05:21,670 --> 00:05:24,576
lined the roadside without end, and tanks

135
00:05:24,596 --> 00:05:27,854
and infantry pushed north along that road.

136
00:05:27,979 --> 00:05:29,802
Simply following that trail was enough

137
00:05:29,822 --> 00:05:32,252
to tell which way the enemy had fled.

138
00:05:32,454 --> 00:05:35,068
Those being chased were in far worse shape.

139
00:05:35,158 --> 00:05:37,357
In an offensive, Chinese soldiers

140
00:05:37,377 --> 00:05:39,406
usually fought carrying only a few

141
00:05:39,426 --> 00:05:41,625
days' worth of food on their backs.

142
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:44,063
Once supplies ran out, the offensive

143
00:05:44,083 --> 00:05:46,648
had no choice but to stop right there.

144
00:05:46,829 --> 00:05:48,607
UN officers had a name for this

145
00:05:48,627 --> 00:05:51,587
weakness: the one-week offensive.

146
00:05:51,673 --> 00:05:53,964
Now that the offensive had broken, all the

147
00:05:53,984 --> 00:05:56,571
Chinese had left was hunger, exhaustion,

148
00:05:56,591 --> 00:05:59,518
and a pursuing army racing up behind them.

149
00:05:59,715 --> 00:06:01,236
Here is the 6th Division's

150
00:06:01,256 --> 00:06:03,090
pursuit, day by day.

151
00:06:03,158 --> 00:06:06,198
Counterattack on May 20th. Mount Kyegwan

152
00:06:06,218 --> 00:06:08,531
and Mount Pukbae on the 25th.

153
00:06:08,551 --> 00:06:12,120
Assembly at Chunchon on the 26th. The attack

154
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:15,217
on the Hwachon power plant on the 27th.

155
00:06:15,263 --> 00:06:17,383
In just eight days, the division

156
00:06:17,403 --> 00:06:19,284
raced from Yangpyong to the

157
00:06:19,304 --> 00:06:21,424
edge of the Hwachon Reservoir.

158
00:06:21,596 --> 00:06:24,404
On May 25th, the 6th Division ran into

159
00:06:24,424 --> 00:06:27,613
a high mountain range north of Kapyong.

160
00:06:27,741 --> 00:06:30,225
Chinese rearguards were dug in on Mount

161
00:06:30,245 --> 00:06:33,964
Kyegwan and Mount Pukbae, buying time.

162
00:06:34,143 --> 00:06:36,630
The division sent the 2nd and 7th Regiments

163
00:06:36,650 --> 00:06:38,542
against the heights to its front.

164
00:06:38,665 --> 00:06:40,602
But the 19th Regiment received a very

165
00:06:40,622 --> 00:06:43,164
different mission: swing wide behind Mount

166
00:06:43,184 --> 00:06:46,436
Pukbae and cut the enemy's line of retreat.

167
00:06:46,621 --> 00:06:48,308
When the 19th Regiment entered

168
00:06:48,328 --> 00:06:51,039
Chiam-ni, the trap snapped shut.

169
00:06:51,118 --> 00:06:53,056
Chinese troops driven down from the

170
00:06:53,076 --> 00:06:54,752
heights found themselves sealed

171
00:06:54,772 --> 00:06:57,086
inside the valley road leading north.

172
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:58,948
In this encirclement alone,

173
00:06:58,968 --> 00:07:00,906
the 6th Division took more than two

174
00:07:00,926 --> 00:07:03,114
thousand six hundred prisoners.

175
00:07:03,252 --> 00:07:05,405
About one thousand seven hundred of them

176
00:07:05,425 --> 00:07:08,296
were reportedly captured by the 19th Regiment,

177
00:07:08,316 --> 00:07:10,320
which held the ring to the end.

178
00:07:10,511 --> 00:07:12,483
Division commander Chang Do-yong

179
00:07:12,503 --> 00:07:14,406
later described the scene.

180
00:07:14,496 --> 00:07:16,172
Chinese soldiers crouching by the

181
00:07:16,192 --> 00:07:18,358
roadside were loaded onto trucks like

182
00:07:18,378 --> 00:07:20,281
so much litter being picked up.

183
00:07:20,330 --> 00:07:22,358
He recalled the extraordinary sight

184
00:07:22,378 --> 00:07:24,566
of a single platoon taking an

185
00:07:24,586 --> 00:07:26,928
entire enemy battalion prisoner.

186
00:07:27,110 --> 00:07:29,162
Archival photographs preserve what

187
00:07:29,182 --> 00:07:31,483
a broken Chinese army looked like.

188
00:07:31,651 --> 00:07:34,147
Soldiers in quilted cotton uniforms,

189
00:07:34,167 --> 00:07:36,822
slumped on the ground. A month earlier,

190
00:07:36,842 --> 00:07:38,588
they had been the attackers.

191
00:07:38,778 --> 00:07:40,888
But at that very moment, a report

192
00:07:40,908 --> 00:07:43,380
reached U.S. IX Corps headquarters.

193
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:45,066
That report would send the 6th

194
00:07:45,086 --> 00:07:47,842
Division toward the Hwachon Reservoir.

195
00:07:48,043 --> 00:07:49,366
Reconnaissance aircraft had

196
00:07:49,386 --> 00:07:51,040
spotted something hard to believe

197
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:53,338
south of the Hwachon Reservoir.

198
00:07:53,434 --> 00:07:55,701
Some ten thousand Chinese troops,

199
00:07:55,721 --> 00:07:57,933
hauling vehicles and field guns,

200
00:07:57,953 --> 00:08:01,111
were moving toward Hwachon in a long column.

201
00:08:01,306 --> 00:08:03,266
While the Chiam-ni area was being

202
00:08:03,286 --> 00:08:05,520
encircled, large forces of the

203
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,512
Chinese 9th Army Group, pulling out of

204
00:08:07,532 --> 00:08:09,662
the east, were also on the move.

205
00:08:09,759 --> 00:08:12,470
To break through the UN ring, they surged

206
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:16,317
past Oum-ni toward the Hwachon power plant.

207
00:08:16,505 --> 00:08:18,596
This reservoir was an artificial lake,

208
00:08:18,616 --> 00:08:22,113
created in 1944 when the Hwachon Dam

209
00:08:22,133 --> 00:08:24,581
was built for hydroelectric power.

210
00:08:24,717 --> 00:08:26,518
Stretching long from east to west

211
00:08:26,538 --> 00:08:28,191
along the river, the lake had

212
00:08:28,211 --> 00:08:30,509
